        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/matchstickman/{size}/1880_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-04-15T21:55:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"MarioFanaticXV\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mariofanaticxv/48/2129_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> MarioFanaticXV:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Where? No spoilers were mentioned, only mechanics. Spoilers refer to plot details that are meant to be surprises.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Even if I agreed with your definition of spoilers (which I don't*), did y ou know that the way you unlock variants is (mostly) through replicating specific things that have happened in the plot of the comics of Sentinels, so would qualify.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Spoilers to me are any information about the game/show/book which lessen the enjoyment.</li>\n</ul>",
